# Vitals environment — copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. NEVER commit real values.

# De-identification salt (ADR 0002). A single shared secret mixed into every patient_key hash so
# the public silver data can't be re-identified by a dictionary/rainbow attack over the (guessable)
# Synthea ID space. Must stay CONSTANT across runs and engines, or patient_key changes and joins
# break. `make setup` generates a random one for you; set it by hand only to match an existing dataset.
# On Databricks, provide it as a job secret (see ADR 0002), not from this file.
VITALS_SALT=change-me-to-a-random-secret
